  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the hard version of the problem. The difference is that you do not remember all array elements correctly, and there are Ai=0A_i = 0Ai​=0. It is worth 60 points in Division 2, 3 and 4, and 100 points in Division 1.**\n\nYou have an array AAA of NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\n\nYou can perform the following operation as many times as you want:\n\n\nChoose L,RL, RL,R such that 1≤L&lt;R≤N1 \\le L &lt; R \\le N1≤L&lt;R≤N and AL=ARA_L = A_RAL​=AR​, then update Ai:=ALA_i := A_LAi​:=AL​ for all L≤i≤RL \\le i \\le RL≤i≤R.\nLet f(A)f(A)f(A) denote the minimum number of distinct elements in the array AAA after applying operations optimally.\n\nIn this version, you have unfortunately forgotten some of the original elements of AAA. The original elements all satisfied 1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N, and if you have forgotten the original value, you are given Ai=0A_i = 0Ai​=0 instead.\n\nFind the minimum value of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all possible original arrays, i.e. minimum f(A)f(A)f(A) by optimally replacing the 000s in AAA with elements in [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible value of f(A)f(A)f(A), after optimal replacement.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\le A_i \\le N0≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105 over all test cases."
    ],
